<http://data.silknow.org/object/45744d3f-a554-3ba4-8cc7-6296b7cbcea3>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Pair of mules with pointed toe, high cut and heels covered with red leather.  The toe pieces are made with beads worked in a woven technique, in shades of yellow, green, red and blue on a white ground arranged to form a pattern of a basket from which floral sprays grow with two birds flanking the top. The upper is bound with gilt ribbon and lined with white kid, canvas and blue silk. A piece of floral brocade, a white ground on which is yellow, green and beige pattern with white flowers, covers the instep. There is white kid lining to the sides of the leather sole."@en , "Pair of women's mules, made in France, 1730s; leather covered with woven beadwork, coloured glass beads."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/56d9ea87-0b78-36a1-ac47-72711725f9fd> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/61c2dc32-3bea-303d-a205-68ff0f2909e1> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Pair of women's mules, made in France, 1730s; leather covered with woven beadwork, coloured glass beads."@en , "Pair of mules with pointed toe, high cut and heels covered with red leather.  The toe pieces are made with beads worked in a woven technique, in shades of yellow, green, red and blue on a white ground arranged to form a pattern of a basket from which floral sprays grow with two birds flanking the top. The upper is bound with gilt ribbon and lined with white kid, canvas and blue silk. A piece of floral brocade, a white ground on which is yellow, green and beige pattern with white flowers, covers the instep. There is white kid lining to the sides of the leather sole."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/45744d3f-a554-3ba4-8cc7-6296b7cbcea3/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/45744d3f-a554-3ba4-8cc7-6296b7cbcea3/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/45744d3f-a554-3ba4-8cc7-6296b7cbcea3/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.102-1971" ;
